{"tmp_id":"B1","title":"Notch calculator helper: RATING_SCALE, notchChange, notchCalculator (src/ratings/notch.mjs) with unit tests","role":"backend","component":"watchlist-domain-lib","context":"WHY: REQ-06-02 asks for a notch calculator helper. The analyst gives a previous and a current rating and gets back the signed notch change, the direction and the resulting Watchlist level (WL 0-4, higher is worse). Other parts of the Watchlist POC import this module, so the export names and signatures below are a fixed contract. B2 (Indicator 12, src/indicators/countryRating.mjs) is built on notchChange from this file. REPO STATE: the repo is empty apart from src/.gitkeep and test/.gitkeep, so there is nothing to stay compatible with. package.json has \"type\":\"module\" and scripts.test = \"node --test\". CONVENTIONS (CLAUDE.md): plain Node 18+ ESM (.mjs). Do not add npm dependencies (package.json must keep no dependencies or devDependencies). Code in src/ratings must be pure functions with no I/O: no imports at all (no node:fs, node:http/https, fetch or process) and no console.* calls. Unit tests use node:test and node:assert/strict and go in test/ratings/notch.test.mjs. Write them test-first. FILE TO CREATE: src/ratings/notch.mjs, which exports exactly these three things. (1) RATING_SCALE = Object.freeze([\"AAA\",\"AA+\",\"AA\",\"AA-\",\"A+\",\"A\",\"A-\",\"BBB+\",\"BBB\",\"BBB-\",\"BB+\",\"BB\",\"BB-\",\"B+\",\"B\",\"B-\",\"CCC+\",\"CCC\",\"CCC-\"]): 19 entries, best first, frozen. Because ESM is strict mode, push or index assignment throws a TypeError. (2) export function notchChange(previous, current) returns the integer index(current) - index(previous) on RATING_SCALE. Positive means downgrade, negative means upgrade, 0 means unchanged. It must never return -0. (3) export function notchCalculator(previous, current) returns a new plain object with exactly the keys { notches, direction, wl }. notches === notchChange(previous, current), signed the same way (human decision CON-interface: BB -> BBB gives -3). direction is \"downgrade\" if notches > 0, \"upgrade\" if notches < 0, otherwise \"unchanged\". wl uses the Indicator 13 thresholds (C2, C6): notches >= 3 -> 2, notches === 2 -> 1, otherwise 0. That means a 1-notch downgrade, any upgrade and an unchanged rating all give 0. Both functions take exactly 2 declared parameters (fn.length === 2). There is no override, options or default parameter (C7). VALIDATION (C1, CON-errors): use one shared internal helper, for example normalizeRating(value, argName). Check typeof value === 'string' first; a non-string (null, undefined, 42, {}) must throw a RangeError, never a TypeError, so do not call .trim() before the check. Then trim and upper-case the value and look it up in RATING_SCALE. Anything not found throws a RangeError. This includes \"\", \"   \", \"BBB +\" (inner space), \"CC\", \"D\", \"NR\", \"AAA+\" and \"Baa1\". It applies to both the previous and the current argument. notchCalculator must get the same RangeError by calling notchChange or the shared helper. Do not wrap or translate the error. The message should name the argument (previous/current) and the offending value, and list the valid ratings (X-error-message). Tests assert the RangeError type only, not the wording. The functions must not change their inputs and must write nothing to stdout or stderr. OUT OF SCOPE: a separate Indicator 13 function; ratings outside the 19 steps (CC/C/D/SD/NR/WD, outlooks, Moody's notation), which are rejected; fetching or pre-filling ratings; UI, CLI or logging. WARNING: the original POC example 'BBB+ -> BB+ = 2 notches -> WL=1' is miscounted. The correct result is 3 notches -> WL=2 (C2). Do not copy the original example into tests. TESTS MUST COVER: every value listed in AC-1, AC-2, AC-5, AC-6, AC-7 and AC-8; the AC-3 normalisation cases for notchChange and notchCalculator; the AC-4 invalid list in both argument positions (with \"BBB\" as the other argument) for notchChange and notchCalculator; the AC-9 exhaustive loop over all 361 pairs (RATING_SCALE x RATING_SCALE); and the notch.mjs part of AC-13 (.length === 2, inputs unchanged, no stdout or stderr output; the no-imports and no-console rule can be checked by reading the source text with node:fs inside the test only).","depends_on":[],"scope":["src/ratings/notch.mjs","test/ratings/notch.test.mjs"],"verify":"node --test test/ratings/notch.test.mjs","qa_scope":["test/integration/ratings/**"],"qa_verify":"node --test test/integration/ratings/notch.integration.test.mjs","acceptance":["AC-1: import RATING_SCALE → deep-equals the 19 ratings AAA..CCC- in C1 order, length 19, Object.isFrozen true, push(\"CC\") throws TypeError and length stays 19, RATING_SCALE[0]=\"X\" throws TypeError and [0] stays \"AAA\"","AC-2: notchChange(\"BBB+\",\"BB+\")→3, (\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\")→2, (\"A\",\"A-\")→1, (\"AAA\",\"CCC-\")→18, (\"BB\",\"BBB\")→-3, (\"CCC-\",\"AAA\")→-18, (\"BBB\",\"BBB\")→0 with Object.is(result,0) true; Number.isInteger on every result","AC-3 (notch part): notchChange(\" bbb+ \",\"bb+\")→3, notchChange(\"\\tAa-\\n\",\"a+\")→1, notchCalculator(\"bbb+\",\"BB+\")→{notches:3,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}","AC-4 (notch part): for notchChange and notchCalculator, each of \"CC\",\"D\",\"NR\",\"AAA+\",\"Baa1\",\"\",\"   \",\"BBB +\",null,undefined,42,{} in the previous and in the current position (other arg \"BBB\") → assert.throws(fn, RangeError) passes (never TypeError, never a returned value)","AC-5: notchCalculator(\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\")→{notches:2,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:1}; (\"BBB+\",\"BB+\")→{notches:3,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}; (\"BB\",\"B\")→{notches:3,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}; (\"AAA\",\"CCC-\")→{notches:18,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}","AC-6: notchCalculator(\"A\",\"A-\") and (\"CCC\",\"CCC-\") → {notches:1,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:0}","AC-7: notchCalculator(\"BB\",\"BBB\")→{notches:-3,direction:\"upgrade\",wl:0}; (\"BBB-\",\"BBB+\")→{notches:-2,…}; (\"A-\",\"A\")→{notches:-1,…}; (\"CCC-\",\"AAA\")→{notches:-18,direction:\"upgrade\",wl:0}","AC-8: notchCalculator(\"BBB\",\"BBB\") and (\"aaa\",\" AAA \") → {notches:0,direction:\"unchanged\",wl:0} with Object.is(notches,0) true","AC-9: for all 361 pairs of RATING_SCALE × RATING_SCALE → Object.keys(r).sort() deep-equals [\"direction\",\"notches\",\"wl\"], r.notches === notchChange(p,c), direction matches the sign, r.wl === (n>=3?2:n===2?1:0)","AC-13 (notch part): notchChange.length === 2 and notchCalculator.length === 2; src/ratings/notch.mjs has no import statements, no node:fs/http/https/fetch/process use and no console.*; calls write nothing to stdout/stderr and leave the arguments unchanged"]},
{"tmp_id":"B2","title":"Indicator 12 country rating change WL: countryRatingChangeWl (src/indicators/countryRating.mjs) with unit tests","role":"backend","component":"watchlist-domain-lib","context":"WHY: REQ-03-12 defines Indicator 12 (Country rating change). It turns the notch change between the previous and current country rating into a Watchlist level of 0, 1 or 2. Other parts of the POC import this function, so its name and signature are a fixed contract. The contract says it is 'built on notchChange'. PREREQUISITE (B1): src/ratings/notch.mjs already exists and exports RATING_SCALE (a frozen array of 19 ratings, AAA..CCC-, best first), notchChange(previous, current) and notchCalculator(previous, current). notchChange returns the integer index(current) - index(previous): positive means downgrade, negative means upgrade, 0 means unchanged. It trims and upper-cases its inputs, and it throws a RangeError for anything that is not one of the 19 ratings, including non-strings such as null, undefined, 42 and {}. Do not edit notch.mjs or its tests. That file is out of this card's scope. If you find a defect there, report it; do not fix it. CONVENTIONS (CLAUDE.md): plain Node 18+ ESM (.mjs), no npm dependencies, pure functions with no I/O in src/indicators, and no console.* calls. Unit tests use node:test and node:assert/strict in test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs. Write them test-first. FILE TO CREATE: src/indicators/countryRating.mjs. Its only import is import { notchChange } from '../ratings/notch.mjs'. It has no other imports and no use of node:fs, http/https, fetch or process. It exports function countryRatingChangeWl(previous, current), with exactly 2 declared parameters (.length === 2). There is no override or edit parameter: the caller passes whichever rating the analyst confirmed (C7). It computes n = notchChange(previous, current) and returns the number n >= 2 ? 2 : n === 1 ? 1 : 0. So a 1-notch downgrade gives 1, a downgrade of 2 or more gives 2, and an upgrade or unchanged rating gives 0. Validation comes from notchChange: let its RangeError reach the caller unchanged (do not catch, wrap or re-validate it in a way that could throw a TypeError). DELIBERATE DIFFERENCE (C6, PRD-conflicts): Indicator 12 thresholds (1 -> 1, 2+ -> 2) are NOT the same as the notchCalculator thresholds (Indicator 13: 1 -> 0, 2 -> 1, 3+ -> 2). Do not harmonise them. AC-12 pins both sets side by side, so this card's tests must import notchCalculator as well. OUT OF SCOPE: fetching or pre-filling the country rating from a public source (C4); override, persistence or audit trail (C7); UI, CLI or logging (C8). WARNING: do not use the original miscounted 'BBB+ -> BB+ = 2 notches' example; BBB+ -> BB+ is 3 notches. FINAL CARD: this card also closes AC-14. From the repo root, `node --test` (= npm test) must exit 0 and run both test/ratings/notch.test.mjs and test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs. package.json must still have no dependencies or devDependencies.","depends_on":["B1"],"scope":["src/indicators/countryRating.mjs","test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs"],"verify":"node --test test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs","qa_scope":["test/integration/indicators/**"],"qa_verify":"node --test test/integration/indicators/countryRating.integration.test.mjs","acceptance":["AC-3 (indicator part): countryRatingChangeWl(\"  a \",\"a-\") → 1","AC-4 (indicator part): for countryRatingChangeWl, each of \"CC\",\"D\",\"NR\",\"AAA+\",\"Baa1\",\"\",\"   \",\"BBB +\",null,undefined,42,{} in the previous and in the current position (other arg \"BBB\") → assert.throws(fn, RangeError) passes (never TypeError, never a returned value/NaN/undefined)","AC-10: countryRatingChangeWl(\"A\",\"A-\")→1, (\"CCC\",\"CCC-\")→1, (\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\")→2, (\"BBB+\",\"BB+\")→2, (\"AAA\",\"CCC-\")→2, each with typeof === \"number\"","AC-11: countryRatingChangeWl(\"BB\",\"BBB\"), (\"A-\",\"A\"), (\"CCC-\",\"AAA\"), (\"BBB\",\"BBB\") → 0; for all 361 RATING_SCALE pairs the result === (n>=2?2:n===1?1:0) with n = notchChange(p,c)","AC-12: notchCalculator(...).wl / countryRatingChangeWl(...) → (\"A\",\"A-\") 0/1, (\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\") 1/2, (\"BBB+\",\"BB+\") 2/2","AC-13 (indicator part): src/indicators/countryRating.mjs imports notchChange from '../ratings/notch.mjs' and nothing else; countryRatingChangeWl.length === 2; no node:fs/http/https/fetch/process use and no console.*; calls write nothing to stdout/stderr and leave the arguments unchanged","AC-14: `node --test` from the repo root exits 0, runs test/ratings/notch.test.mjs and test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs (together covering AC-1..AC-13), and package.json still has no dependencies/devDependencies"]}
]

