ings/**"],"qa_verify":"node --test test/integration/ratings/notch.integration.test.mjs","acceptance":["AC-1: import RATING_SCALE → deep-equals the 19 ratings AAA..CCC- in C1 order, length 19, Object.isFrozen true, push(\"CC\") throws TypeError and length stays 19, RATING_SCALE[0]=\"X\" throws TypeError and [0] stays \"AAA\"","AC-2: notchChange(\"BBB+\",\"BB+\")→3, (\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\")→2, (\"A\",\"A-\")→1, (\"AAA\",\"CCC-\")→18, (\"BB\",\"BBB\")→-3, (\"CCC-\",\"AAA\")→-18, (\"BBB\",\"BBB\")→0 with Object.is(result,0) true; Number.isInteger on every result","AC-3 (notch part): notchChange(\" bbb+ \",\"bb+\")→3, notchChange(\"\\tAa-\\n\",\"a+\")→1, notchCalculator(\"bbb+\",\"BB+\")→{notches:3,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}","AC-4 (notch part): for notchChange and notchCalculator, each of \"CC\",\"D\",\"NR\",\"AAA+\",\"Baa1\",\"\",\"   \",\"BBB +\",null,undefined,42,{} in the previous and in the current position (other arg \"BBB\") → assert.throws(fn, RangeError) passes (never TypeError, never a returned value)","AC-5: notchCalculator(\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\")→{notches:2,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:1}; (\"BBB+\",\"BB+\")→{notches:3,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}; (\"BB\",\"B\")→{notches:3,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}; (\"AAA\",\"CCC-\")→{notches:18,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:2}","AC-6: notchCalculator(\"A\",\"A-\") and (\"CCC\",\"CCC-\") → {notches:1,direction:\"downgrade\",wl:0}","AC-7: notchCalculator(\"BB\",\"BBB\")→{notches:-3,direction:\"upgrade\",wl:0}; (\"BBB-\",\"BBB+\")→{notches:-2,…}; (\"A-\",\"A\")→{notches:-1,…}; (\"CCC-\",\"AAA\")→{notches:-18,direction:\"upgrade\",wl:0}","AC-8: notchCalculator(\"BBB\",\"BBB\") and (\"aaa\",\" AAA \") → {notches:0,direction:\"unchanged\",wl:0} with Object.is(notches,0) true","AC-9: for all 361 pairs of RATING_SCALE × RATING_SCALE → Object.keys(r).sort() deep-equals [\"direction\",\"notches\",\"wl\"], r.notches === notchChange(p,c), direction matches the sign, r.wl === (n>=3?2:n===2?1:0)","AC-13 (notch part): notchChange.length === 2 and notchCalculator.length === 2; src/ratings/notch.mjs has no import statements, no node:fs/http/https/fetch/process use and no console.*; calls write nothing to stdout/stderr and leave the arguments unchanged"]},
{"id":"T-02","title":"Indicator 12 country rating change WL: countryRatingChangeWl (src/indicators/countryRating.mjs) with unit tests","role":"backend","agent":"backend-dev","component":"watchlist-domain-lib","state":"ready","attempts":0,"notes":[],"context":"WHY: REQ-03-12 defines Indicator 12 (Country rating change). It turns the notch change between the previous and current country rating into a Watchlist level of 0, 1 or 2. Other parts of the POC import this function, so its name and signature are a fixed contract. The contract says it is 'built on notchChange'. PREREQUISITE (T-01): src/ratings/notch.mjs already exists and exports RATING_SCALE (frozen array of 19 ratings, AAA..CCC-, best first), notchChange(previous, current) and notchCalculator(previous, current). notchChange returns the integer index(current) - index(previous): positive = downgrade, negative = upgrade, 0 = unchanged. It trims and upper-cases its inputs and throws a RangeError for anything that is not one of the 19 ratings, including non-strings (null, undefined, 42, {}). Do not edit notch.mjs or its tests (out of this card's scope); if you find a defect there, report it. CONVENTIONS (CLAUDE.md): plain Node 18+ ESM (.mjs), no npm dependencies, pure functions with no I/O in src/indicators, no console.* calls. Unit tests use node:test and node:assert/strict in test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs. Write them test-first. FILE TO CREATE: src/indicators/countryRating.mjs. Its only import is import { notchChange } from '../ratings/notch.mjs'. No other imports and no use of node:fs, http/https, fetch or process. It exports function countryRatingChangeWl(previous, current), exactly 2 declared parameters (.length === 2), no override or edit parameter (C7). It computes n = notchChange(previous, current) and returns n >= 2 ? 2 : n === 1 ? 1 : 0 (1-notch downgrade gives 1, 2+ gives 2, upgrade or unchanged gives 0). Validation comes from notchChange: let its RangeError reach the caller unchanged (do not catch or wrap it). DELIBERATE DIFFERENCE (C6, PRD-conflicts): Indicator 12 thresholds (1 -> 1, 2+ -> 2) are NOT the notchCalculator thresholds (Indicator 13: 1 -> 0, 2 -> 1, 3+ -> 2). Do not harmonise them. AC-12 pins both side by side, so this card's tests must import notchCalculator as well. OUT OF SCOPE: fetching or pre-filling the country rating (C4); override, persistence or audit trail (C7); UI, CLI or logging (C8). WARNING: BBB+ -> BB+ is 3 notches, not 2. FINAL CARD: this card also closes AC-14. From the repo root, `node --test` (= npm test) must exit 0 and run both test/ratings/notch.test.mjs and test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs. package.json must still have no dependencies or devDependencies.","depends_on":["T-01"],"scope":["src/indicators/countryRating.mjs","test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs"],"verify":"node --test test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs","qa_scope":["test/integration/indicators/**"],"qa_verify":"node --test test/integration/indicators/countryRating.integration.test.mjs","acceptance":["AC-3 (indicator part): countryRatingChangeWl(\"  a \",\"a-\") → 1","AC-4 (indicator part): for countryRatingChangeWl, each of \"CC\",\"D\",\"NR\",\"AAA+\",\"Baa1\",\"\",\"   \",\"BBB +\",null,undefined,42,{} in the previous and in the current position (other arg \"BBB\") → assert.throws(fn, RangeError) passes (never TypeError, never a returned value/NaN/undefined)","AC-10: countryRatingChangeWl(\"A\",\"A-\")→1, (\"CCC\",\"CCC-\")→1, (\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\")→2, (\"BBB+\",\"BB+\")→2, (\"AAA\",\"CCC-\")→2, each with typeof === \"number\"","AC-11: countryRatingChangeWl(\"BB\",\"BBB\"), (\"A-\",\"A\"), (\"CCC-\",\"AAA\"), (\"BBB\",\"BBB\") → 0; for all 361 RATING_SCALE pairs the result === (n>=2?2:n===1?1:0) with n = notchChange(p,c)","AC-12: notchCalculator(...).wl / countryRatingChangeWl(...) → (\"A\",\"A-\") 0/1, (\"BBB+\",\"BBB-\") 1/2, (\"BBB+\",\"BB+\") 2/2","AC-13 (indicator part): src/indicators/countryRating.mjs imports notchChange from '../ratings/notch.mjs' and nothing else; countryRatingChangeWl.length === 2; no node:fs/http/https/fetch/process use and no console.*; calls write nothing to stdout/stderr and leave the arguments unchanged","AC-14: `node --test` from the repo root exits 0, runs test/ratings/notch.test.mjs and test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs (together covering AC-1..AC-13), and package.json still has no dependencies/devDependencies"]}
]}

